  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`.\n\n**Cause:** in `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py`), a child context inherited the parent's whole `default_map` instead of the entry for its own command name. Subcommand options were therefore looked up in the wrong dict level and never matched.\n\n**Fix:** the child now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, so `default_map={\"foo\": {\"name\": \"mapped\"}}` applies to subcommand `foo`.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_default_map_subcommand` in `tests/test_defaults.py`. It checks that the nested entry is applied and that a top-level key is not wrongly applied to the subcommand.\n\nThe full suite passes: 1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed.",
